    "rationale": "GU (n_train 708, the smallest client) is the most extreme client on two independent screens. In the round-20 client_performance table its observed prevalence (0.197) is well above the global model's mean prediction (0.130), giving CITL -0.067 (flagged citl z=-3.1), while its AUC (0.815) is normal, which matches a prevalence shift rather than label noise. In client_updates its mean cosine to the median update is the lowest of all 52 clients (0.143, flagged mean_cos z=-3.2), consistent with a client whose labels pull it away from the federation. Both signals are only around 3 sigma and the client is small, so this is a low-confidence lead. Budget was exhausted before it could be confirmed with a per-round prevalence query. Other screens (feature_summary, subgroup_outcomes, drift_by_round, attribution_churn) showed only small-client noise with no consistent pattern, so no other client was reported.",
